// B = c + d
// C = a - b
// D = c - d

// Then:
// (A - B) * x = dx
// (C - D) * y = dy

// Also:
// |C| <= A and C ≡ A (mod 2)
// |D| <= B and D ≡ B (mod 2)
// A, B >= 0

// From (A - B) * x = dx:
// If x == 0, then dx must be 0, and A - B can be anything (but A, B >= 0)
// If x != 0, then A - B = dx / x, which must be an integer

// Similarly for y.

